  "All 10 programs are CICS online programs (has_exec_cics true).",
  "XCTL/dynamic LINE: for 'EXEC CICS' on one line and 'XCTL PROGRAM(...)' on the next (COMEN01C:184/185 and 201/202, COTRN00C:192/193 and 518/519, etc.) I used the first physical line of the statement (the EXEC CICS line) for both evidence and the ?dynamic id. If the adjudicated convention is the XCTL keyword line, those ids shift by +1.",
  "CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM has no VALUE in COCOM01Y (app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy:24) and is a MOVE receiver everywhere, so every XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM) gets one edge per distinct literal moved to it anywhere in that program plus one ?dynamic edge. MOVE CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (COTRN01C:119, COTRN02C:140, COUSR02C:116, COUSR03C:115) is not a literal and gives no candidate edge.",
  "COMEN01C:156 and :184 XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-MENU-OPT-PGMNAME(WS-OPTION)) are subscripted: dynamic only, no candidate edges (menu literals live in COMEN02Y).",
  "EXEC CICS INQUIRE PROGRAM(...) at COMEN01C:148 is not CALL/LINK/XCTL and gets no edge.",
  "CORPT00C:517 EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') is a transient data queue, not a FILE/DATASET operation, so no data edge. CORPT00C also holds JCL text in string literals (line 94 '//STEP10 EXEC PROC=TRANREPT') that is not a statement.",
